title: Electoral Agreement
subtitle: A joint list for the coming Sejm election, while the lists are open.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: parliament_affairs
card-image: img/poster_2.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishGovernment.listAgreementAvailable(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card parliament.list_agreement (technical reference 6.2, 6.5; card catalogue 7.7). One choice; the
// confirmation spends this month's action even when the partners refuse; looking is free.
for (var id of PolishGovernment.LIST_ORDER) {
    Q['pl_list_' + id + '_reason'] = PolishGovernment.listStatus(Q, id).reason;
}
!}

= A joint list?

The lists for the coming Sejm election are open until the end of the month before the vote. Without an agreement PPS stands alone with its full programme and all its own candidates; refusing an alliance brings no bonus.

A joint list counts the votes of its parties together in the seat method, and shares its seats in proportion to their votes. Each party keeps its own club after the election and may vote differently; a list gives no ministry and binds nobody to a later cabinet. Each partner answers once, by the same evaluation as a cabinet offer. PPS can agree at most one list for this election.

- @left_peasant
- @labour
- @centrolew_early
- @peasant
- @easy_discard

@left_peasant
title: A joint list of PPS and PSL Wyzwolenie
subtitle: Land reform with equal access and protection of labour; seats shared in proportion to votes.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.listStatus(Q, 'left_peasant').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_list_left_peasant_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
var record = PolishGovernment.proposeList(Q, 'left_peasant');
Q.pl_list_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_list_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
Q.pl_list_name = PolishGovernment.LIST_OPTIONS.left_peasant.name;
!}
go-to: result

